        "original_id": "8bb982bb-49ae-5c79-82b2-92d0159f7eb4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edwin Forrest, William Charles Macready, Catherine Norton Sinclair, William Creswick, Edwin Booth, Fanny Kemble\n- Events: Astor Place Riot\n- Places: Astor Opera House, Manhattan, New York City, London, Britain, the U.S., Australia\n- Topics: acting, divorce, Shakespearean roles, melodrama\n\nFacts:\n- On May 10, 1849, the Astor Place Riot occurred at the now-demolished Astor Opera House in Manhattan, New York City.\n- The Astor Place Riot left at least 25 people dead and more than 120 injured.\n- Edwin Forrest's feud with the British actor William Charles Macready caused the deadly Astor Place Riot of 1849.\n- Catherine Norton Sinclair's sensational divorce from Edwin Forrest captivated the American public in the mid-1800s.\n- William Creswick was a popular tragedian on the London stage.\n- William Creswick appeared with leading actors of his day, including William Charles Macready, Edwin Booth, and Fanny Kemble.\n- William Creswick was well known for Shakespearean and melodrama roles in Britain, the U.S., and Australia.",
